Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.880
PRIYA PATEL: Hi, everybody.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.650
Welcome to Cloud OnAir, live
webinars from Google Cloud.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.000
We're hosting webinars
every Tuesday.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.610
My name is Priya Patel.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.580
And today, we'll be talking
about transforming your content

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.370
management strategy
with Box and G Suite.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.870
You can ask questions
anytime on the platform,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.810
and we have Googlers on
standby to answer them.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.760
So let's get started.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.980
My name is Priya Patel.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.680
And I'm the Group Product
Marketing Manager at Box,

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.620
focused on our partnerships
and integrations.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.490
I'm excited to be joined shortly
by John Lake, Vice President

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.890
of Enterprise Applications
from DocuSign,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.050
who is going to join
us live for a Q&amp;A

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.040
to learn about how DocuSign
is using both Box and G Suite

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.920
today, as well as the Box
for G Suite integration,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.836
to be more productive.

00:00:50.836 --> 00:00:53.340
By way of agenda today,
we're going to be covering--

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.230
I know it's a mixed
audience of folks

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.900
who might be familiar
with Box and folks

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.400
who aren't as familiar.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.980
So I want to spend some time
giving a brief introduction

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.120
into Box.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.800
And then, of course, we want
to give an overview of the Box

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.890
for G Suite integration
and provide a live demo

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.220
so you can see it in action.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.010
And then we're going to bring
John Lake up from DocuSign

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.370
to do a customer
spotlight Q&amp;A. And we also

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.100
want to make sure that we have
time for audience questions

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.200
as well.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.100
So starting with Box, I
want to just kick this off

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.830
by talking about
the mission of Box.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.830
Over the past 13 years, we've
heard from many companies

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.770
like Nike, Coca-Cola, and GE.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.940
And they've all said
a very similar thing,

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.310
which is that they want
to be more efficient.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.800
They want to be faster.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.900
But sometimes technology
stands in the way.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.530
And so, at Box, our
mission is very simple--

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.220
to power how the
world works together.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.085
And we work with
companies around the globe

00:01:52.085 --> 00:01:54.060
of every industry--

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.410
as you can see here, even some
of the most highly regulated

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:01.340
industries like the public
government, financial services

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:04.610
companies, and companies
in the health care space.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.580
We have 87,000 customers today.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.259
And we're really
excited to be helping

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:14.780
to drive digital transformation
for all of these customers.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.780
Digital transformation is on
every company's mind today.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.530
It's incredibly important to
be agile in an increasingly

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.470
competitive, fast-paced
business environment.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.230
And how we collaborate
and manage our information

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.140
is really at the core of
digital transformation.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:33.080
Because information touches
every business process,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.780
it runs through every
employee at a company,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.720
and is incredibly critical
to getting business done.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.740
But unfortunately, the
way that our information

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.590
is managed today is fragmented.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:48.440
And this is because of the
way that content strategies

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.450
have evolved in a very
fragmented way over time.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:56.060
So starting in the '90s, you
had file shares, network drives,

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.330
even physical media,
going to the post office

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.880
to transmit content.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.980
And enterprise content
management solutions

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.610
such a Documentum and
SharePoint and OpenText

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.600
evolved to provide one central
repository for your content

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.510
that could be easily
searched and indexed.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.120
But these were not built
for the end user in mind.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.230
And because they
weren't as easy to use,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.700
they never evolved beyond a
few departmental use cases.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.610
And then, with the
rise in mobility

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.220
and the need to be
able to work on the go,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.500
consumer file sync
and share tools

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.960
that were very easy
to use and intuitive,

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.010
such as Dropbox and
Microsoft OneDrive cropped up

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.250
as well to meet the new
demands of the workforce.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.220
And then, at the same time,
application development

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.630
became popular again.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:47.570
And you have a lot of companies
building their own custom

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.250
applications on platforms such
as AWS and Microsoft Azure.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.060
And we've also seen a rise
of line of business cloud

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.300
applications such as
Salesforce and Workday,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.900
new cloud tools that enhance
collaboration, such a Slack

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.580
and Workplace by Facebook.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.800
And all of this means
that your content

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.770
is fragmented across all
of these different systems

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.780
and applications today.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.460
For those dialed
in, I'd like you

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.990
to just take a
look at this slide

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:19.130
and think about how many
different applications you're

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.779
using at your
organization today,

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:23.370
such as those listed here.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.980
And you're probably
using multiple today.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.870
So what if you had
one platform that

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.510
worked for all of your content?

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.360
That's Cloud Content
Management from Box.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.150
It's one platform,
born in the cloud that

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.700
enables seamless
and secure internal

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.730
and external collaboration,
provides a single source

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.760
of truth for content across
your best-of-breed applications

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:52.020
because it integrates seamlessly
across your applications.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.670
It automates business workflows
across the extended enterprise,

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:57.860
leverages advanced
machine learning

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.350
and artificial
intelligence technologies

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.990
from all the major vendors,
including Google Cloud

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:06.950
Platform, to help automate
business workflows

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.560
and provide security and
compliance for every industry

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:14.520
and geo without
sacrificing simplicity.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.990
I'd like to give an overview of
what the Box platform provides.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.810
At the core, you have
the content capabilities,

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.780
the ability to seamlessly
collaborate internally

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.280
and externally across
teams, automate workflows,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.640
apply machine learning and
intelligence to your content,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.760
but there is a lot more
to that that Box offers.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.100
Box has several
native applications.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.070
I'll just touch upon
a few listed here.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.150
Box Drive, which enables
you to stream your Box

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:50.520
files on your desktop to imitate
a network drive experience--

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.320
so taking up very
little space, but being

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.790
able to easily access your
files in a very familiar way.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.000
Box Relay, which provides
workflow capabilities that

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.250
are very end-user focused,
very simple for the end

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.390
user to set up to automate
manual, repeatable workflows.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.670
Box Notes, which is
a really easy way

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:12.150
for teams to
collaborate in real time

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:15.510
when they're in meetings to
capture notes as well as action

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:16.560
items.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.450
And Box Capture, which enables
you to take photos on the go

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.960
when you're at work.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.040
This is great for
mobile field teams

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.710
with all of those photos
stored securely into Box

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:31.060
versus on your personal device.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:33.480
Those are just some
examples of Box apps.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.000
And as I mentioned, Box
integrates seamlessly

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.250
across a multitude of tools.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:43.320
We have over 1,400 cloud
application integrations today.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.600
Of course, G Suite, which
we're going to focus on today,

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.250
but we also integrate
with Office 365,

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.710
messaging and collaboration
tools such as Slack,

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.770
Workplace by Facebook, line
of business applications,

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.020
such as Salesforce
and ServiceNow,

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:02.070
as well as e-signature solutions
such as DocuSign and Adobe

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:02.580
Sign--

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.260
we're excited to
have John join us

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.470
later on to talk a bit more
about what DocuSign does--

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.860
as well as workflow and
business process management

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:14.460
tools, such as Nintex and Pega.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:18.030
And then Box has a
robust APIs and SDKs

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:22.770
that enable companies to build
on the Box platform with Box

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:27.480
as the content layer powering
applications such as client

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.730
portals, when you
have lots of documents

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:33.880
that you're sharing between
internal and external parties--

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:37.170
this is a very popular use
case for wealth management--

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.860
mobile field support for
companies that have a big

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.530
employee base in the field,
custom digital process--

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.440
this is great for
marketing teams

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:52.320
to easily share content across
internal and external parties.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.860
And then I really want to
highlight the last piece, which

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:57.510
is important, which
is that all of this

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.320
resides on a layer of
security and compliance

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.740
that makes this all safe
to reside in the cloud.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.840
So Box, starting
with Insights, Box

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.810
has over 80 different
reports that we

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:16.950
offer to IT admins to get really
granular reporting into how

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.890
content is being shared and
managed across the organization

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.140
and outside.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.710
With Box Zones, we offer
the ability for companies

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:29.280
to select where their data
is stored to comply with data

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.860
residency requirements.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.150
We offer multiple layers
of protection and DLP--

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.470
also, from the
governance perspective,

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:44.430
the ability to apply legal holds
and apply retention policies

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.700
on your content, on your
files, on your folders.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.950
And then, through
our KeySafe product,

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:53.280
we allow customers to
manage their own encryption

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:56.500
keys for ultimate privacy.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.590
And so I hope this gives
you a sense for what

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:00.780
the Box platform provides--

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.480
pretty robust capabilities
beyond just kind

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.200
of sharing and
managing your content,

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.950
but providing a variety
of apps, integrations,

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.410
and a platform offering
to be able to do more

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.610
with your content.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.630
So now I'd like to dive into the
Box for G Suite integration--

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:21.450
why we're all here today.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.390
A little bit of
background about Box--

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.470
Box and Google have
been strategic partners

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:26.730
for a few years now.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.730
And we're working
together to transform

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.340
the way organizations
collaborate and do work

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.540
in the cloud.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.780
And we're excited to be
deepening our partnership

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:39.900
through new
integrations over time.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.790
So we launched our Hangouts Chat
integration earlier this year.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.540
Docs, Sheets, and Slides, which
is the focus of today's webinar

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.120
is publicly available
today through beta

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.150
and will be available
generally, to the public,

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.800
by the end of this year.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.430
And I'll provide more details
on how to get this integration.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:02.280
We're also going to be
launching our Gmail integration

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.350
by end of this year as well.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.310
We announced this and
shared it at Google Next

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.660
a couple of months ago.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.860
And I'll also be providing more
details on that integration

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:14.880
later on.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:20.460
We also integrate with Google
Cloud and the Google Cloud

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:23.310
Platform to provide Google
Machine Learning capabilities

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.680
to Box customers
to apply to content

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:31.800
to automate business processes.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:33.350
So Box for G Suite--

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.590
just by way of an overview
of what this provides,

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.870
we're bringing the
rich experience

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:43.010
of Google Docs, Sheets, and
Slides directly into Box.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:47.450
And so this means that you can
seamlessly leverage Google's

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.700
familiar editing
experience from within Box,

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.120
so you can create a new Google
Docs, Sheets, and Slides

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.220
while ensuring your
content is organized

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.260
and easily discoverable.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.630
You can collaborate in
real time with Google's

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.150
rich real-time
editing capabilities

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.760
in Google Sheets
and Slides, being

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.100
able to see edits that
are happening in real time

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.370
with all changes
instantly saved into Box,

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.890
and you can maintain
enterprise-level standards--

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:15.740
so ensuring your content meets
the security, compliance,

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.590
and governance requirements
of any industry

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:22.930
with our robust
security infrastructure.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.170
So in terms of key features
that I'll be highlighting

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:26.820
in the demo shortly--

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:30.480
you can easily create new
Docs, Sheets, and Slides

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.800
with any edits that you make to
these documents instantly saved

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.090
into Box.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:39.780
And you can also see
version history in Box

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:44.310
like you can with any other
document that's managed in Box.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:49.170
And you get the robust
security that I mentioned,

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:52.080
our governance
capabilities, to any files

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.550
that are saved in Box.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.190
And John from DocuSign
will be joining us shortly

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.960
to provide a live
customer viewpoint.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:04.040
But I wanted to highlight one
of our other joint customers

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.540
of the Box for G
Suite integration--

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:08.260
Indiana University.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.240
G Suite is widely used
across the education space.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.220
And they're using
Box for G Suite

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:17.220
across 100,000 faculty and
students to share syllabi

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:21.790
and to manage
educational content.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:26.500
And so with that, I'm
going to go into the demo.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:30.720
So this is what the Box
experience looks like.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.570
Over here, you can easily
search for any files.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:35.820
You can search by
file type, by the date

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.580
it's uploaded, by title.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:43.950
On the left, you can easily
access your recent files.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:48.090
You can easily see notifications
if someone left comments

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:51.360
for you to look at a document.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.099
All your Box Notes
would be stored here.

00:12:53.099 --> 00:12:55.140
You can also favorite
documents so you can easily

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.275
refer to them.

00:12:56.275 --> 00:12:58.320
And then, over here, you have--

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.860
so I'm in a Launch folder.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:02.790
I'm in marketing.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:07.860
And I often collaborate with
my product manager counterparts

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.290
in this folder.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.160
And so I can see
everyone who's here.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.690
I can easily share the folder.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.270
Depending on who I
want to share it with,

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:21.150
I can edit permission
levels, stop them

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:23.610
from being able to edit,
maybe just enabling them

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.700
to view or preview or download.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.770
So Box offers pretty granular
permission capabilities there.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:35.100
And I'm going to go ahead and
go into a product spec document

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.660
because my team, I
know, has been editing.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.500
You can see here, they're in
