where they could collaborate
internally, relatively

00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:04.530
simply, easily, quickly
across platforms was great.

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:07.115
But then, of course, you have
a lot of input and feedback

00:28:07.115 --> 00:28:09.020
from your external agencies.

00:28:09.020 --> 00:28:11.480
So again, targeting
a good use case,

00:28:11.480 --> 00:28:13.430
getting some early
quick wins with it

00:28:13.430 --> 00:28:17.870
to build some momentum with it,
and then just staying adamant,

00:28:17.870 --> 00:28:20.330
almost, about the
progression of rolling this

00:28:20.330 --> 00:28:25.610
out and then turning down
and rolling off of those

00:28:25.610 --> 00:28:26.300
file servers.

00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:28.490
I think overall, over the
course of the execution,

00:28:28.490 --> 00:28:31.160
we moved about-- a little over
40 terabytes worth of data

00:28:31.160 --> 00:28:31.670
into Box.

00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:32.936
PRIYA PATEL: That's great.

00:28:32.936 --> 00:28:34.310
And that's actually--
you touched

00:28:34.310 --> 00:28:38.000
upon something that comes
up a lot with customers

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:41.780
who have selected Box is that,
with their previous content

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:46.430
platforms, it's not so easy
to share files externally.

00:28:46.430 --> 00:28:48.290
So as an example,
some customers who

00:28:48.290 --> 00:28:51.470
might be using the
Office Suite, they

00:28:51.470 --> 00:28:53.835
have to toggle between
OneDrive and SharePoint.

00:28:53.835 --> 00:28:56.690
They have to use SharePoint
for external sharing, OneDrive

00:28:56.690 --> 00:28:58.871
for internal sharing.

00:28:58.871 --> 00:29:02.732
So that's great that
you highlighted that.

00:29:02.732 --> 00:29:04.190
And then the other
thing you noted,

00:29:04.190 --> 00:29:06.980
which also comes up
a lot, is the need

00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:09.380
for change management
and to provide training

00:29:09.380 --> 00:29:12.380
to your employees to drive
adoption of these tools.

00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:14.750
I think Box is
very user-friendly,

00:29:14.750 --> 00:29:16.880
as is DocuSign, as is G Suite.

00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:18.679
But it's important to
have those early wins

00:29:18.679 --> 00:29:20.220
as well to share
with your employees.

00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:21.136
JOHN LAKE: Absolutely.

00:29:21.136 --> 00:29:22.036
Totally agree.

00:29:22.036 --> 00:29:24.400
PRIYA PATEL: So another
question that came in,

00:29:24.400 --> 00:29:27.020
"Does this integration
requires a Google account?"

00:29:27.020 --> 00:29:28.310
That's a great question.

00:29:28.310 --> 00:29:33.740
This integration is available
to customers with paid G Suite

00:29:33.740 --> 00:29:34.884
accounts.

00:29:34.884 --> 00:29:36.800
So as long as you have
a paid G Suite account,

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:38.810
you're eligible to
use this integration,

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:40.100
and it's completely free.

00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:45.110
"Can multiple users
simultaneously

00:29:45.110 --> 00:29:47.330
edit a single document?"

00:29:47.330 --> 00:29:47.830
Yes.

00:29:47.830 --> 00:29:48.460
Absolutely.

00:29:48.460 --> 00:29:51.070
That's one of the great
benefits of G Suite,

00:29:51.070 --> 00:29:53.920
enabling that real-time
collaboration.

00:29:53.920 --> 00:29:55.930
And so they can edit it.

00:29:55.930 --> 00:29:59.825
They can resolve comments with
all changes saved into Box.

00:30:03.220 --> 00:30:04.960
"Which Google editors
are included?"

00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:08.500
Google Docs, Sheets, and Slides,
and as I mentioned and showed

00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:12.970
in the demo, you can
actually convert Office files

00:30:12.970 --> 00:30:16.330
into G Suite files,
and any edits

00:30:16.330 --> 00:30:19.280
will be saved back into
the original file format.

00:30:24.350 --> 00:30:26.450
And then, someone
is asking about how

00:30:26.450 --> 00:30:29.250
to access the public beta.

00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:35.650
So the public beta, if you
go to box.com/partner/google,

00:30:35.650 --> 00:30:39.440
there will be a link to be
able to sign up for the beta.

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.810
But it will be generally
available to the public

00:30:41.810 --> 00:30:43.310
by end of year, which is great.

00:30:43.310 --> 00:30:45.920
Because anyone will be able
to-- if you're a Box admin--

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:47.820
you can just enable it
in your admin console.

00:30:54.580 --> 00:30:56.080
OK.

00:30:56.080 --> 00:30:58.420
Those are all of the questions.

00:30:58.420 --> 00:31:02.110
Stay tuned for the next session,
Extending Google's Grab and Go

00:31:02.110 --> 00:31:03.910
Program to Your Business.

00:31:03.910 --> 00:31:05.326
John, thank you for joining us.

00:31:05.326 --> 00:31:06.075
It was a pleasure.

00:31:06.075 --> 00:31:07.260
JOHN LAKE: Thank you.

00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:09.370
PRIYA PATEL: Thank
you, everyone.

